BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film screening: Persepolis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T200000
UID:6a2700ca703c3363002d2179@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In memory of the author Marjane Satrapi\, join us for a screen
 ing of Persepolis\, based on her award winning graphic novel.\nThe poignan
 t story of a young girl coming-of-age in Iran during the Islamic Revolutio
 n. Clever and fearless\, she outsmarts the "social guardians" and discover
 s punk\, ABBA and Iron Maiden. Yet when her uncle is senselessly executed 
 and as bombs fall around Tehran in the Iran/Iraq war\, the daily fear that
  permeates life in Iran is palpable.\n2007\, 96 minutes\nRated 14+\nDrop i
 n – no registration needed.\nPersepolis\nPersepolis
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2700ca703c3363002d2179
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T163000
UID:69583000c719ac98c335c8c7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nTHHC can be contacted at 416-285-8070.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69583000c719ac98c335c8c7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
