BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T130000
UID:69ff4aa4703c336300268210@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nTue
 sday\, July 7 from 10AM - 12PM.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Tuesday\,\no
 nce a week for 8 weeks\, July 14 - September 1\n. Registration closes afte
 r week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and
  refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be
  available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerste
 in Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely res
 ponsible for the protection of \npersonal information collected through th
 e program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ff4aa4703c336300268210
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Craft Movie Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T200000
UID:6a3eebd8f56bd86e00b955cd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a cozy Craft & Movie evening. Bring your unfinishe
 d craft or start something new while we relax together and enjoy a feel-go
 od film! Settle in with your project as we watch a lighthearted comedy\, d
 ramedy\, or romcom\, perfect for sparking creativity and conversation. It
 ’s a great way to unwind\, connect\, and make progress on your craft.
LOCATION:Junction Triangle\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3eebd8f56bd86e00b955cd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SP Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T150000
UID:698bcaa1cbf6405d356706f4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discuss diverse and inclusive titles from a variety of genres 
 on the fourth Thursday of every month!\nThis month we will be discussing y
 our current or recent reads.\nJoin us for a\nBYOB (Bring Your Own Book) me
 eting\n\, where we swap stories about what we're reading. Simply show up w
 ith a book you've read recently to share a quick review and connect with o
 ther readers. It’s the perfect way to discover your next favorite book w
 ithout the pressure of a deadline.\nRegistration is required and begins Ju
 n. 25\, 2026.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on
  this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Lib
 raries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only
  be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Que
 stions about how the library handles your information can be directed to A
 nswerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\
 , Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Canoe Table\, center of branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698bcaa1cbf6405d356706f4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SP Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T150000
UID:698bcb20cbf1533ca536cabd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discuss diverse and inclusive titles from a variety of genres 
 on the fourth Thursday of every month!\nThis month we will be discussing\n
 All This and More\nby Peng Shepherd.\nDesperate for a second chance\, fort
 y-five-year-old Marsh joins\nAll This and More\n\, a global sensation usin
 g quantum technology to let contestants revise their histories. But as she
  crafts a seemingly perfect existence\, the glossy promise of the show beg
 ins to fracture\, revealing a reality that may be too good to be true. Thi
 s gripping story puts the reader in the driver’s seat\, challenging you 
 to navigate the fine line between fixing the past and losing oneself entir
 ely.\nPick up a physical copy at the branch before the meeting\, or find c
 opies through our website in various formats. Registration is required and
  begins Jul. 23\, 2026.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Canoe Table\, center of branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698bcb20cbf1533ca536cabd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
