BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Swati Namjoshi
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T235959
UID:6a24321846d5f64f7dce27e6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, works by artist Swati Namjoshi
  are on display at Bloor Gladstone Library in an exhibit.\nSwati is an Ind
 ian multidisciplinary artist\, now based in Toronto\, making it her new ho
 me. She strongly believes in the power of stories and works towards illus
 trating authentic & mindful representations of cultures\, characters\, pla
 ces\, and perspectives. In her curious exploration of a gendered society\
 , Swati creates autobiographical digital illustrations in black & white\; 
 a vulnerable expression of her experiences as an artist\, a woman\, and a\
 nmother.\nSwati states "The parallels I see across cultures and the inter
 sectionality in our identity influence my art and the way I explore and em
 brace diversity.  The human experience is far more shared than it is div
 ise\, and I paint to contribute to the love rather than the hate. My style
  exhibits emotive characters embedded in their whisical worlds.  I believ
 e presenting vulnerable experiences through hopeful illustrations that toy
  with reality and exaggeration\, could nurture a sense of belonging and co
 mmunity."\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toro
 nto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work 
 at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cu
 ltural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be v
 iewed during Bloor/Gladstone branch's open hours. Please check the\nBloor
 /Gladstone branch\npage before you visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage c
 redit: Swati Namjoshi\; Bounce\; Medium: Digital Illustration Printed on P
 aper
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a24321846d5f64f7dce27e6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
