BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Weston Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T110000
UID:693f0f5294297d36009feee8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join our book club for engaging discussions\, new book recomme
 ndations\, and a fun way to connect with fellow book lovers! Whether you'r
 e a lifelong reader or just getting started\, we welcome all to share thei
 r thoughts and dive into exciting reads together.\nHere are the upcoming m
 eeting dates and titles:\nJune 20: The sleeping car porter\nJuly 18: The
  Immortalists\nAugust 15: How it all began\nSeptember 19: Bobbi Lee: Ind
 ian Rebel\nOctober 17: Me before you\nNovember 21: The Riveter\nDecember 1
 9: More than enough\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informat
 ion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publ
 ic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wil
 l only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluatio
 n. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directe
 d to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge S
 treet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Weston\, Youth Hub Area. Main Floor.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/693f0f5294297d36009feee8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Be Ready\, Toronto! Emergency Preparedness Workshop for Individual
 s and Households
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T140000
UID:6a39c518c78687f2fd2df413@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Emergencies can happen anywhere at any time. In Canada\, we fa
 ce numerous hazards\, including wildfires\, flooding\, heatwaves\, and ear
 thquakes. The Be Ready workshop aims to raise individual and household eme
 rgency preparedness.\nIn this free workshop facilitated by the\nToronto Em
 ergency Management Division of the City of Toronto\n\, in partnership with
  the\nCanadian Red Cross\n\, participants will learn about:\nThe potential
  hazards and risks in their area\nHow to create an emergency plan\nHow to 
 assemble an emergency kit\nThe importance of social and support networks d
 uring emergencies\nFree program. Registration required! For more informati
 on\, please contact the branch.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Eatonville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a39c518c78687f2fd2df413
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Mahjong
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260727T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260727T120000
UID:696ecaa576261f2800655b61@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. Meet new folks\, build social connections\, 
 and tell us\n about programs and services you would like to see in the nei
 ghbourhood!\nDrop-in. No registration required.\nSnacks and refreshments a
 re provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at t
 he program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre
 's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:City Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696ecaa576261f2800655b61
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
