BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SP Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T150000
UID:698bcb8ea5d80ac49270fa0c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discuss diverse and inclusive titles from a variety of genres 
 on the fourth Thursday of every month!\nThis month we will be discussing\n
 Soft as Bones\nby Chayna Marie Sage.\nChyana Marie Sage weaves a poetic me
 moir about overcoming the legacy of generational trauma through the power 
 of traditional Cree healing. Tracing the pain from her father’s incarcer
 ation and the Sixties Scoop to her own struggles with addiction\, she exam
 ines the dark footprint of colonialism on her family. Ultimately\, this is
  a story of hope\, braiding personal narrative with ancient ceremony to re
 claim a fractured past.\nPick up a physical copy at the branch before the 
 meeting\, or find copies through our website in various formats. Registrat
 ion is required and begins Aug. 27\, 2026.\nInformation Collection Notice:
 \nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public
  Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(
 d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\,
  delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inf
 ormation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416
 -397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Canoe Table\, center of branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698bcb8ea5d80ac49270fa0c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
