BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T130000
UID:69fe21b61ed2c2bb2e2ca858@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nThu
 rsday\, July 23\, 10:00am-12:00pm.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Thursday\
 ,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, July 30-September 17\, 10:00am-1:00pm\n. Regi
 stration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be p
 rovided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingre
 dient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collabo
 ration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis C
 entre is solely responsible for the protection of \npersonal information c
 ollected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Parkdale\, Auditorium A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe21b61ed2c2bb2e2ca858
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Heart Health Conversations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T190000
UID:6a3040ac43b41b3d006e8fd1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Heart-related illnesses remain one of the leading causes of de
 ath in Canada\, yet many of the factors that influence heart health are wi
 thin our control. Understanding these factors and knowing what steps you c
 an take to manage them can play an important role in supporting long-term 
 cardiovascular health.\nWhat to Expect:\nUnderstanding Risk Factors:\nLear
 n about common factors that can impact heart health and how to recognize t
 hem.\nPrevention Strategies:\nExplore practical steps that can help suppor
 t heart health and reduce risk.\nHealthy Lifestyle Practices:\nLearn about
  practices that contribute to overall cardiovascular well-being.\nAccessin
 g Resources and Support:\nLearn about available services and supports that
  can help you maintain and support your heart health.\nThis session will b
 e led by health professionals from\nLAMP Community Health Centre\n\, who 
 will provide practical information and guidance to help you better underst
 and your options and take the next steps.\nThis program is presented by To
 ronto Public Library in collaboration with the\nWest Toronto Ontario Healt
 h Team\n(OHT)\, a network of over 40 local health and social service provi
 ders working together to improve the health and well-being of communities 
 in West Toronto.\nYour Health Matters\nThis program is part of Toronto Pub
 lic Library’s\nYour Health Matters\ninitiative\, which offers trusted he
 alth programs and resources to help people make informed decisions about t
 heir health. Learn more by exploring the\nYour Health Matters web page\n.\
 nReserve Your Spot Today!\nThis virtual event is free to join but registra
 tion is required.\nPlease register on Eventbrite\n.\nOnce registered\, you
 ’ll receive an email with details on how to join the session.\nWe can’
 t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3040ac43b41b3d006e8fd1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
