BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Your Health Matters: Staying Healthy in a Changing Climate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T200000
UID:6a502411fb418a280099da6b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Climate change is already affecting our health in a variety of
  ways\, from extreme heat and poor air quality to more frequent extreme we
 ather events. Join us to learn how these environmental changes can affect 
 your health and discover practical steps you can take to stay safe and pro
 tect your well-being.\nThis session will explore:\nHow climate change and 
 extreme weather can impact human health\nHow to recognize poor air quality
 \, high UV ratings\, and other environmental health risks\nPractical strat
 egies to help protect yourself and reduce the risk of heat- and climate-re
 lated health complications\nResources and services available to help you s
 tay safe\, including the Heatwave Registry and options for connecting with
  primary care\nAbout the Speaker\nDr. Samantha Green is a family physician
  at St. Michael's Hospital and Inner City Health Associates in Toronto. Sh
 e is also an Assistant Professor in the Department of Family and Community
  Medicine at the University of Toronto and President of the Canadian Assoc
 iation of Physicians for the Environment.\nThis program is presented by To
 ronto Public Library in collaboration with the\nWest Toronto Ontario Healt
 h Team\n(OHT)\, a network of over 40 local health and social service provi
 ders working together to improve the health and well-being of communities 
 in West Toronto.\nYour Health Matters\nThis program is part of Toronto Pub
 lic Library’s\nYour Health Matters\ninitiative\, which offers trusted he
 alth programs and resources to help people make informed decisions about t
 heir health. Learn more by exploring the\nYour Health Matters web page\n.\
 nReserve Your Spot Today!\nThis virtual event is free to join but registra
 tion is required.\nPlease register on Eventbrite\n.\nOnce registered\, you
 ’ll receive an email with details on how to join the session.\nWe can’
 t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a502411fb418a280099da6b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
