BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Funding\, Grants & Growth Opportunities For Women Entrepreneurs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T200000
UID:6a2d5e757550c8bf9f5d1521@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Finding the right funding can be one of the biggest challenges
  facing entrepreneurs. Fortunately\, there are a growing number of grants\
 , programs\, and support organizations designed to help women entrepreneur
 s start and grow their businesses.\nThis workshop provides an overview of 
 funding pathways\, grant opportunities\, community resources\, and busines
 s support programs. Participants will leave with a better understanding of
  what resources are available and where to begin their search for funding 
 and growth opportunities.\nAll sessions are interactive and participants a
 re encouraged to bring questions related to their own business or entrepre
 neurial goals.\nMeet the Resident\n: Melanie Cruickshank is a founder and 
 brand-side operator with over 15 years of experience building\, launching\
 , and scaling beauty and personal care brands. As the founder of da lish c
 osmetics\, she led everything from product development and retail strategy
  to e-commerce growth and national partnerships. Known for her hands-on\, 
 no-nonsense approach\, Melanie brings a founder’s accountability and a d
 eep understanding of what it takes to build brands that perform in market.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2d5e757550c8bf9f5d1521
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260831T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260831T150000
UID:6a2b299bdcc1022f00394af9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nJoin us at the crafts & games ta
 ble\, or for a community walk (weather permitting).\nVisit with a therapy 
 dog!\nHippie is here on June 15\, 29 + July 13\, 27 + August 10\, 24.\nOzz
 y is here June 22 + July 6\, 20 + August 17\, 31.\nSnacks and refreshments
  are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at
  the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Cent
 re's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2b299bdcc1022f00394af9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building Your Own Website for Small Business (Focus: Women Entrepr
 eneurs)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T200000
UID:6a2720c943b41b3d006cd0a1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Having a personal website is essential for any small business.
  This\n8-week course\nwill cover everything from the basic fundamentals an
 d tools of WordPress all the way to the platform's advanced features that 
 support promoting and running a small business. Participants are encourage
 d to bring their own laptop\, but it is not required to attend.\nRegistrat
 ion is required for the full series. Participants are expected to attend a
 ll sessions on the following dates:\nJuly 22\nJuly 29\nAugust 5\nAugust 12
 \nAugust 19\nAugust 26\nSeptember 2\nSeptember 9\nThis program is hosted b
 y the Business\, Science and Technology department. Please visit the 3rd f
 loor service desk or call (416) 393-7149 for more information.\nThis progr
 am is part of the\n"Building your own Website for Small Business" Program 
 Series (Women Entrepreneurs stream)\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Learning Centre 2\, 1st Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2720c943b41b3d006cd0a1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
