BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Modern Marketing: Building Awareness Without a Big Budget
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T200000
UID:6a2c8a9b1e67cd9cb3398f8c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Many entrepreneurs assume they need a large marketing budget t
 o grow their business. The reality is that some of the most effective mark
 eting strategies cost very little and rely more on consistency\, creativit
 y\, and connection.\nJoin us for a discussion on modern marketing approach
 es including content creation\, community building\, partnerships\, referr
 als\, and creator-led marketing. Participants will explore practical ways 
 to increase visibility\, attract customers\, and build momentum without re
 lying heavily on paid advertising.\nAll sessions are interactive and parti
 cipants are encouraged to bring questions related to their own business or
  entrepreneurial goals.\nMeet the Resident\n: Melanie Cruickshank is a fou
 nder and brand-side operator with over 15 years of experience building\, l
 aunching\, and scaling beauty and personal care brands. As the founder of 
 da lish cosmetics\, she led everything from product development and retail
  strategy to e-commerce growth and national partnerships. Known for her ha
 nds-on\, no-nonsense approach\, Melanie brings a founder’s accountabilit
 y and a deep understanding of what it takes to build brands that perform i
 n market.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2c8a9b1e67cd9cb3398f8c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Reflections of Nature by Brenda Sherwood
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260706T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T235959
UID:6a4c16519aae2bdc2800805f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, works by artist Brenda Sherwood
  are on display at Don Mills Branch.\nBrenda Sherwood is a professional ph
 otographer represented by Getty Images. She has had four exhibits and her 
 photos that were sold are in private collections. She is also a Filmmaker 
 and won a Gemini for her film\, The Bellringer. She is a member of the Aca
 demy of Canadian Cinema and Television.\nBrenda Sherwood received her Hono
 rs Bachelor of Arts in 2021. She graduated at University of Toronto with a
  HBA in Digital Enterprise Management Specialist and a minor in Art Histor
 y.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Pu
 blic Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at loc
 ations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural
  interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed 
 during branch open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Don Mills
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4c16519aae2bdc2800805f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Data Analytics Essentials Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T153000
UID:6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61ddc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about data analytics? Let's take a free
  online course together in a welcoming space!\nA\nlearning circle\nis a st
 udy group\, guided by library staff\, for people who want to take a free o
 nline course together in a supportive and welcoming environment.\nOrganiza
 tions all over the world recognize the value of analytics. Together\, we'l
 l learn about the essential tools used in this field.\nIn this 12-week lea
 rning circle\, we will work through the Data Analytics Essentials course f
 rom Cisco Networking Academy. We will explore the fundamental tools of a d
 ata analyst\, including how to:\ntransform\, organize and visualize data w
 ith spreadsheet tools like Excel\nquery data from a relational database us
 ing SQL\nimprove data presentations using business intelligence tools like
  Tableau\nWe will meet weekly\,\nin-person\,\nevery Tuesday afternoon\, Se
 ptember 15 - December 8\, 2-3:30 PM (12 sessions).\nParticipants are expec
 ted to commit to the duration of the course and attend sessions on a weekl
 y basis.\nLearners who complete the course will be able to:\nearn a digita
 l badge\ndownload a certificate of completion
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61ddc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google AI Essentials: In Person Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T150000
UID:6a32e00d4407827f8aa595a0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about artificial intelligence or want to learn practic
 al AI skills for work and personal use? Join our staff-facilitated learnin
 g circle to complete the self-paced Google AI Essentials specialization.\n
 This 10-hour introductory-level specialization\, offered through Coursera\
 , is available for free to learning circle participants. It is made up of 
 five courses\, each containing four units that consist of short videos\, a
 rticles\, assignments and a short multiple-choice quiz.\nBy completing the
  specialization\,\nyou will learn:\nHow AI works\nHow to write effective p
 rompts\nHow to use generative AI tools responsibly\nHow to identify AI's p
 otential biases and avoid harm\nHow to stay up to date with AI news\nAfter
  you complete the course\, you earn a Google certificate and a badge to sh
 are with others\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary staf
 f for people who want to complete the Google AI Essentials specialization 
 together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work together thr
 ough course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to attending a
 ll four learning circle sessions.\nNo AI experience is required.\nHow to J
 oin\na Learning Circle:\nRegister once on the first session of this event 
 series\, in order to attend all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid em
 ail address\n.\nA valid TPL library card is required for online circles.
 \nAttend all four sessions in person at\n[\nEthennonnhawahstihnen']\n.\nRe
 gistration is a two-step procedure. First\, participants must complete the
 ir registration through this page. After this step\, library staff will fo
 llow up to request additional information in order to complete the registr
 ation.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this f
 orm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries 
 Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be use
 d for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions 
 about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerli
 ne staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toron
 to ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Ethennonnhawahstihnen'
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a32e00d4407827f8aa595a0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
