BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monthly Movie Screening: I Like Movies
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T200000
UID:69e17936fca21471b7ef70d9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This month's feature:\nI Like Movies\nEnjoy a night at the mov
 ies! Join us for a free movie on the big screen in our accessible theatre.
 \nDescription: Socially awkward 17-year-old cinephile\, Lawrence Kweller\
 , is self-absorbed and movie-obsessed. Fully convinced he can earn $90\,00
 0 to achieve his dream of attending film school at NYU\, he gets a part-ti
 me job at Sequels video store. There older store manager\, Alana\, takes h
 im under her wing. Meanwhile Lawrence sabotages every high school relation
 ship he has with his narcissistic film snobbery. Faced with the impending 
 reality of university life\, Lawrence must change his ways.\nThis film is 
 rated 14A. 99 minutes. Start time is 6:00 pm. Drop in. All are welcome!
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Theatre (lower level)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e17936fca21471b7ef70d9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
