BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea and Movies: The Hours (2002)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T150000
UID:6a4aa1b5ddf70344004443ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us every month for a free afternoon movie. Tea & coffee w
 ill be served. No registration required.\nThis month’s film: The Hours (
 2002)\nThis gripping drama follows a single day in the lives of three wome
 n from different generations\, all deeply connected by Virginia Woolf’s 
 novel\nMrs. Dalloway\n. As Woolf herself struggles to write the book in th
 e 1920s\, a repressed 1950s housewife and a contemporary 1990s woman navig
 ate their own inner turmoils\, searching for love\, freedom\, and meaning 
 in a poignant exploration of the human spirit.
LOCATION:Thorncliffe
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4aa1b5ddf70344004443ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Travels of Odysseus
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T190000
UID:6a2035d8748daf857d5ab2fb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In Homer's ​\nThe Odyssey\n\, Odysseus narrates his wanderin
 gs on the way home from Troy to Ithaca to his hosts the Phaeacians. The ta
 les are often full of wondrous material: exotic peoples\, monsters\, gods 
 and goddesses\, and dangerous natural phenomena. Once back home\, however\
 , Odysseus\, in disguise as a stranger\, tells false travel tales with rea
 l geography and the real peoples of the Mediterranean.\nIn this lecture Pr
 of. Jonathan Burgess will discuss the theme of travel in\nThe Odyssey\n\, 
 focusing on the paradox between the fantastical true travels of Odysseus a
 nd the realistic "lying tales" on Ithaca\, as well as the persistent urge 
 to identify the "real-world" locations of Odysseus' return through unlikel
 y theories and maps.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall (first floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2035d8748daf857d5ab2fb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Club de lecture de S. Walter Stewart: Cercle littéraire
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T200000
UID:69fa4612e13d3b4603b36404@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:*English text follows*\nAimez-vous lire en français? Avez-vou
 s envie de participer à des discussions autour des livres dans une ambian
 ce conviviale et détendue?\nRejoignez notre club de lecture en français
 !\nOn se réunit pendant l'été pour discuter de nos lectures récentes 
 et de nos coups de coeur littéraires.\nA\nucun livre n'est assigné pour 
 cette séance\n. Soyez préparés à discuter d'un livre (ou de plusieurs!
 ) de votre choix que vous avez lu pendant votre temps libre.\nLe Club de L
 ecture régulier reprendra en septembre.\nSi vous voulez en savoir plus su
 r nos clubs de lectures\, veuillez nous envoyer un courriel à\nprogrammes
 enfrancais@tpl.ca\nSi vous souhaitez pratiquer votre français mais que vo
 us avez plutôt un niveau débutant\, nous vous encourageons à découvrir
  également nos\ncercles de conversation\n.\nLe sous-titrage en direct ou 
 automatique\, l’interprétation en langue des signes\, les services d’
 intervenant\, ou les services d’accompagnement sont disponibles sur dema
 nde. Veuillez soumettre votre demande au moins deux semaines à l’avance
  à :\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.\nDo you like to read in French? Wo
 uld you like to participate in discussions in French about books in a fri
 endly and relaxed environment?\nJoin our French Book Club!\nWe will be mee
 ting over the summer to discuss recent reads and literary favourites.\nNo 
 particular book is assigned for this session.\nBe prepared to discuss a bo
 ok (or several!) of your choice that you read in your free time.\nThe regu
 lar French Book Club will resume in September.\nIf you would like to know 
 more about our French Book Clubs\, please send us an e-mail at\nprogrammes
 enfrancais@tpl.ca\nIf you would like to practice your French but you ident
 ify more as a beginner\, we encourage you to discover our\nFrench Conversa
 tion Circles\n.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fa4612e13d3b4603b36404
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
