BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Starting and Sustaining a Business (Business Law)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260721T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260721T190000
UID:69d542c7f29b90618efda044@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Calling all business owners and entrepreneurs! Growing your bu
 siness takes hard work and perseverance. Don't let legalities hold you bac
 k. In this presentation\, we will discuss the proper approach under Ontari
 o business law. From incorporation\, to contracts\, to business structurin
 g\, we will go over everything you need to know so you can stay focused on
  what your business does best.\nThis presentation will be led by Samuel Mi
 chaels\, a Toronto-based corporate lawyer who has been running his own law
  firm\, SM Legal\, since 2017.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d542c7f29b90618efda044
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Photography by Alex Curren
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T235959
UID:6a1ee10d4407827f8aa208a6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, the works of artist Alex Curren
  are on display at\nDeer Park branch\n.\n"Alex Curren is a Toronto-born ar
 tist working across film\, photography\, and design. After studying animat
 ion in Ottawa\, he returned to the city where he grew up and continued his
  studies in film at York. He has served as cinematographer on several shor
 t films and a feature by an emerging filmmaker. He has previously sold sil
 kscreen prints\, drawings\, and handmade goods. He now works at a midtown 
 photo lab\, continuing to explore everyday beauty through analog and digit
 al processes."\n"This project began when I moved back to Toronto in 2017. 
 I told a friend the city felt unphotogenic. He replied\, “It’s easy to
  make art in a far-off place— every blade of grass feels exotic.” Coul
 d I find beauty in the familiar? These film photographs\, all taken near t
 he Deer Park Library\, reflect my love of walking\, photography\, and the 
 quiet intersections of nature and the urban. This collection is an invitat
 ion to pause and see Toronto anew\, a city known for its hectic pace.\nThi
 s exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Lib
 rary provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations a
 cross the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interes
 ts of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during D
 eer Park's open hours. Please check the\nDeer Park branch\npage before you
 r visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Artist: Alex Curren\nTitl
 e of Piece: Picasso Rock (Oriole Park)\nMedium: Photography (film)\nSize
 /Dimensions: Large
LOCATION:Deer Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1ee10d4407827f8aa208a6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
