BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Know Your Customer\, Know Your Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T200000
UID:6a3318e243b41b3d006f3e33@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Here's the mistake most new entrepreneurs make: they build som
 ething and then go looking for someone to buy it. We're flipping that.\nIn
  this interactive workshop\, participants will explore how to define and u
 nderstand their customer. Learn how a clear understanding of your audience
  can help you create stronger marketing\, refine your products and service
 s\, set effective pricing\, and deliver a more compelling pitch.\nMeet the
  Resident:\nVivian Kaye is a serial entrepreneur and business mentor who b
 ootstrapped KinkyCurlyYaki to seven figures without outside funding. Over 
 15 years\, she has mentored 300+ entrepreneurs\, recently facilitating wor
 kshops for FoundHers Innovation Labs and Humber College's Entrepreneurship
  Program.\nFeatured in The New York Times\, Toronto Star\, and on CityTV's
  Cityline\, Vivian has partnered with brands including Shopify\, Amazon\, 
 and American Express Canada. Her direct\, practical approach helps early-s
 tage Black entrepreneurs navigate the realities of building sustainable bu
 sinesses without traditional support systems.\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registratio
 n\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your 
 information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 
 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Meeting Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3318e243b41b3d006f3e33
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
