BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Your Health Matters: Heatwave Registry
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260715T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260715T150000
UID:6a46b4d20e851028002ecb7f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Hot weather can pose serious health risks\, particularly for o
 lder adults and those who may be more vulnerable to extreme heat.\nJoin a 
 representative from the West Toronto Ontario Health Team to learn about th
 e Heatwave Registry and how it can help support people during periods of e
 xtreme heat.\nThe session will also share practical tips for staying safe 
 and healthy throughout the summer.\nThis program is presented by Toronto P
 ublic Library in collaboration with the\nWest Toronto Ontario Health Team\
 n(OHT)\, a network of over 40 local health and social service providers wo
 rking together to improve the health and well-being of communities in West
  Toronto.\nYour Health Matters\nThis program is part of Toronto Public Lib
 rary’s\nYour Health Matters\ninitiative\, which offers trusted health pr
 ograms and resources to help people make informed decisions about their he
 alth. Learn more by exploring the\nYour Health Matters web page\n.\nReserv
 e Your Spot Today!\nThis free\, in-person event is open to everyone.\nRegi
 stration is preferred\, but drop-ins are welcome.\nRegister on Eventbrite 
 to reserve your spot.\nWe can't wait to see you there!
LOCATION:Runnymede
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a46b4d20e851028002ecb7f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
