BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dufferin/St. Clair Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260901T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260901T200000
UID:6958356a1e64afd01e520490@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us the first Tuesday of each month to discuss books in a 
 fun and friendly atmosphere.\nCopies are available for pickup at the Duffe
 rin/St. Clair branch each month\, or place your own hold to have a copy se
 nt to your closest branch.\nJuly:\nNo Two Persons\nby Erica Bauermeister\
 nAugust:\nThe Covenant of Water\nby Abraham Verghese\nSeptember:\nPurity\
 nby Jonathan Frazen\nOctober:\nThe Edible Woman\nby Margaret Atwood\nNovem
 ber:\nSlammerkin\nby Emma Donoghue\nDecember:\nWhat We Can Know\nby Ian M
 cEwan
LOCATION:Dufferin/St.Clair\, Earlscourt Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6958356a1e64afd01e520490
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Princess of Dreams: Mixed Media Portrait
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260908T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260908T150000
UID:6a19a9c752c88111723b8bbf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A captivating mixed media portrait of a dream-filled princess 
 adorned with flowers woven into her hair. Layers of texture\, color\, and 
 delicate details create a magical atmosphere\, celebrating beauty\, imagin
 ation\, and the gentle connection between nature and fantasy. Her floral c
 rown symbolizes hope\, creativity\, and the blossoming of dreams\, invitin
 g viewers into a world of wonder and enchantment.\nThis is a Drop-In progr
 am for Adults and Seniors.\nNo registration required.\nSpace is limited. A
 ll materials are provided
LOCATION:Locke
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a19a9c752c88111723b8bbf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mentorship & Community: Why Relationships Matter In Business
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T200000
UID:6a2d5e8b8d1b82ca9f79aec3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:No entrepreneur builds a business alone. Mentors\, peers\, col
 laborators\, and professional networks can all play an important role in h
 elping entrepreneurs navigate challenges and uncover new opportunities.\nT
 his\n session explores the value of mentorship and community in \nentrepre
 neurship. Participants will learn where to find mentors\, how to \nbuild m
 eaningful professional relationships\, and how to create a support\n netwo
 rk that can contribute to long-term growth and success.\nAll\n sessions ar
 e interactive and participants are encouraged to bring \nquestions related
  to their own business or entrepreneurial goals.\nMeet the Resident\n: Mel
 anie Cruickshank is a founder and brand-side operator with over 15 years o
 f experience building\, launching\, and scaling beauty and personal care b
 rands. As the founder of da lish cosmetics\, she led everything from produ
 ct development and retail strategy to e-commerce growth and national partn
 erships. Known for her hands-on\, no-nonsense approach\, Melanie brings a 
 founder’s accountability and a deep understanding of what it takes to bu
 ild brands that perform in market.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2d5e8b8d1b82ca9f79aec3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T160000
UID:69fd150743b41b3d0064f5ea@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Dufferin/St. Clair library and its neighbourhood is home t
 o a variety of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to exp
 lore the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recogni
 ze different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological imp
 ortance.\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nRe
 gistration is required.\nThe tour will start and end at the Dufferin/St. 
 Clair library ramp entrance and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urb
 an Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route.
  Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. glove
 s/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This program ta
 kes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, regist
 rants will be notified of an alternative date.\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Dufferin/St.Clair\, Library ramp entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fd150743b41b3d0064f5ea
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
