BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Money Basics\, Getting Paid & Finding Funding
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T200000
UID:6a331e058ea300e2631e7d51@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Nobody got into business to be broke. But a lot of people stay
  broke in business because nobody taught them the basics - how money moves
 \, what to track\, how to set yourself up so you actually keep what you ea
 rn. And then there's the question everyone has but nobody asks out loud: w
 here do I find money to grow this thing?\nThis workshop explores the fund
 amentals of business finance\, including how to manage your money\, track 
 key financial information\, and identify funding opportunities. Discover g
 rants and resources that can help support and grow your business.\nMeet th
 e Resident:\nVivian Kaye is a serial entrepreneur and business mentor who 
 bootstrapped KinkyCurlyYaki to seven figures without outside funding. Over
  15 years\, she has mentored 300+ entrepreneurs\, recently facilitating wo
 rkshops for FoundHers Innovation Labs and Humber College's Entrepreneurshi
 p Program.\nFeatured in The New York Times\, Toronto Star\, and on CityTV'
 s Cityline\, Vivian has partnered with brands including Shopify\, Amazon\,
  and American Express Canada. Her direct\, practical approach helps early-
 stage Black entrepreneurs navigate the realities of building sustainable b
 usinesses without traditional support systems.\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Meeting Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a331e058ea300e2631e7d51
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T130000
UID:69fe21b61ed2c2bb2e2ca860@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nThu
 rsday\, July 23\, 10:00am-12:00pm.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Thursday\
 ,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, July 30-September 17\, 10:00am-1:00pm\n. Regi
 stration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be p
 rovided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingre
 dient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collabo
 ration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis C
 entre is solely responsible for the protection of \npersonal information c
 ollected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Parkdale\, Auditorium A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe21b61ed2c2bb2e2ca860
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
