BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Future Entrepreneur: Creator Economy\, Multi-Income Streams & 
 Modern Business Models
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T200000
UID:6a2d5e657550c8bf9f5d1517@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Entrepreneurship is evolving. Today's founders are building bu
 sinesses through consulting\, digital products\, content creation\, commun
 ity building\, partnerships\, and other innovative revenue streams.\nThis 
 session explores how modern entrepreneurs are adapting to a changing busin
 ess landscape and creating multiple pathways for growth. Participants will
  discover emerging business models\, explore opportunities for diversifica
 tion\, and gain insight into the future of entrepreneurship.\nAll sessions
  are interactive and participants are encouraged to bring questions relate
 d to their own business or entrepreneurial goals.\nMeet the Resident\n: Me
 lanie Cruickshank is a founder and brand-side operator with over 15 years 
 of experience building\, launching\, and scaling beauty and personal care 
 brands. As the founder of da lish cosmetics\, she led everything from prod
 uct development and retail strategy to e-commerce growth and national part
 nerships. Known for her hands-on\, no-nonsense approach\, Melanie brings a
  founder’s accountability and a deep understanding of what it takes to b
 uild brands that perform in market.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2d5e657550c8bf9f5d1517
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
