BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Between the Lines Bookclub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T200000
UID:6962837f91e4576f847bd101@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Become a page-turner by joining the Between the Lines Book Clu
 b! Here\, we embark on a new chapter with every read\, diving into a world
  of endless possibilities. From gripping thrillers to heartwarming coming-
 of-age tales\, or a sprinkle of fantasy adventures\, there's something for
  everyone. Whether you're a die-hard fan of one genre or love mixing thing
 s up\, you'll find a place here to discuss\, share\, and connect with fell
 ow readers. Ready to explore different worlds and discover your next favor
 ite book? Join us and let?s turn the page together!\nFriday June 19\n: The
  Alchemist\nby Paulo Coelho\nThe Alchemist by Paulo Coelho is a simple yet
  deeply philosophical novel about following your dreams. It tells the stor
 y of Santiago\, a young shepherd who embarks on a journey from Spain to th
 e Egyptian desert in search of treasure. Along the way\, he encounters men
 tors and challenges that teach him about listening to his heart\, recogniz
 ing opportunity\, and pursuing his “Personal Legend.” Blending element
 s of fable\, spirituality\, and adventure\, the book explores themes of de
 stiny\, courage\, and the idea that the universe supports those who truly 
 commit to their dreams.\nFriday July 17\n: The Lost Bookshop by Evie Woods
 \nThe Lost Bookshop\nis a richly layered novel that weaves together myster
 y\, historical fiction\, and magical realism through the lives of characte
 rs connected across time by a hidden bookshop. Moving between past and pre
 sent\, the story explores themes of identity\, resilience\, love\, and the
  search for belonging\, while revealing how books can offer escape\, under
 standing\, and the courage to change one’s life. At its heart\, the nove
 l is a reflection on the quiet magic of stories and the unexpected ways th
 ey shape the people who find them.\nIf you need help getting a copy of the
  book or have any questions\, please contact us at sastaff@tpl.ca or 416-3
 93-7653. Copies of the monthly titles are available at the circulation des
 k.
LOCATION:Sanderson\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6962837f91e4576f847bd101
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
