BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Craft and Chat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T190000
UID:69a0928f4a9fd98b7f80bfea@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Feeling crafty?\nDo you like to crochet\, embroider\, knit\, j
 ournal\, or something else entirely? If you are looking to chat with some 
 fellow crafters while enjoying your favourite hobby\, come join our Craft 
 and Chat.\nCraft and socialize in a friendly and welcoming environment. Un
 leash your talent\, express your creativity\, and make new friends.\nJoin 
 us weekly for a fun hour of creativity. All skill levels welcome.\nA limit
 ed supply of materials will be available\, so please bring your own suppli
 es and a small project\, if you have them.\nLimited instruction available 
 for beginners in cross-stitch.\nDrop in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Centre of room at Canoe Table
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a0928f4a9fd98b7f80bfea
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T130000
UID:69a0e9296724c63d00f579aa@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on Sat
 urday\, June 13\, 2026\, 10 am-12 pm.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Saturd
 ay\,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, June 20-August 15\, 2026\, 10 am-1 pm\n. 
 There will be no session on Saturday\, August 1. Registration closes afte
 r week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and
  refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be
  available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerste
 in Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely res
 ponsible for the protection of \npersonal information collected through th
 e program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Children's Program Room - Main floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a0e9296724c63d00f579aa
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
