BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Northern District Book Club—Evenings
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260715T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260715T200000
UID:69bc1041b6c4ac1fedc6d29b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a friendly\, spirited discussion of a different bo
 ok on the third Wednesday of each month. We read an eclectic mix of mostly
  contemporary fiction.\nThere is also an afternoon session to discuss the 
 same book on the second Wednesday of each month at 2:00 p.m.  You are we
 lcome at either or both!\nMay 20\, 2026:\nSea of Tranquility\nby Emily St.
  John Mandel\nJune 17\, 2026:\nPrairie Edge\nby Conor Kerr\nJuly 15\, 2026
 :\nLiberation Day\nby George Saunders\nNote:\nno August meeting\nSeptember
  16\, 2026:\nOrbital\nby Samantha Harvey\nOctober 21\, 2026:\nMaybe You Sh
 ould Talk to Someone\nby Lori Gottlieb\nNovember 18\, 2026:\nStone Yard De
 votional\nby Charlotte Wood\nDecember 16\, 2026:\nPerfection\nby Lorenzo P
 atronico
LOCATION:Northern District\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bc1041b6c4ac1fedc6d29b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
