BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dystopia Nonfiction Book Club: Nexus
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T153000
UID:69bda11c491b809c6f21df63@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us each month to discuss issues in politics and society\,
  and explore how powerful forces are exploiting our world and dystopian im
 aginings are becoming present-day realities.\nAugust’s book is\nNexus: A
  Brief History of Information Networks from the Stone Age to AI\nby histor
 ian and philosopher Yuval Noah Harari. Copies of the book are available in
 \nprint\n\,\neBook\nand\neAudiobook\nformats. Book club attendees are enc
 ouraged to read the book in advance of the meeting.\nNexus describes how 
 “information networks have made\, and unmade\, our world… despite all 
 our discoveries\, inventions\, and conquests\, we now find ourselves in an
  existential crisis. The world is on the verge of ecological collapse.” 
 Harari argues that AI is “a species-level threat\, given its ability to 
 amplify misinformation\, accelerate conflict and ignore human cultural con
 straints such as the threat of mutually assured destruction. The wider his
 torical lens on AI and machine learning grounds his overall message of cau
 tion in a deep human context. He pushes back against what he calls a ‘na
 ive view’ of information – thinking that information corresponds to an
  objective reality\, and that more information will lead to more accurate 
 knowledge. He demonstrates how the explosive growth of silicon-based infor
 mation networks has driven alternate realities and conspiratorial thinking
  at the cost of social cohesion and individual liberty.” – Times Liter
 ary Supplement\nDrop in. No registration required.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Discussion Room\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bda11c491b809c6f21df63
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Concerts - Dabbie Danbrook and Steve Raiman: Music of Relax
 ation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T200000
UID:6a19e78552c88111723ba602@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for a live concert of peaceful Japanese Shakuha
 chi Flute music played by Debbie Danbrook. Accompanied on keyboards by St
 eve Raiman.\nThis Healing Music has been composed specifically to help lis
 teners relax.\nTuesday\, July 14\, 2026\,\n7:00 p.m. – 8:00 p.m.\nBeeton
  Hall\,\nToronto Reference Library
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Han
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a19e78552c88111723ba602
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
