BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Start & Grow Your Business with Enterprise Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T183000
UID:6a4f9d2164ed854800a4d585@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Information session on how to start\, plan\, finance and grow 
 your very own small business.\nOwning a business is a dream for many peopl
 e. Every new business starts with an idea. This interactive presentation w
 ill give an overview of how to make it happen and the opportunity to ask q
 uestions related to your business. An advisor from Enterprise Toronto will
  present an overview of information related to the business planning proce
 ss\, evaluating a business idea\, financing\, marketing planning\, busines
 s structures\, regulatory requirements\, and more.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4f9d2164ed854800a4d585
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: WORDLY
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T203000
UID:6a46864648c98c3600a3e5bd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, the works of artist Jacinto Sal
 cedo are on display at Leaside branch in an exhibit titled\nWORDLY\n.\nJac
 into Salcedo is a Venezuelan-Canadian award-winning graphic designer whose
  practice is rooted in simplicity\, resourcefulness\, and emotional impac
 t. For him\, design is more than aesthetics—it is strategy\, vision\, an
 d problem-solving. Salcedo brings discipline\, curiosity\, and a critical 
 eye to his work. With a passion for creating meaningful visual experience
 s\, he seeks to deliver creative solutions that bridge function and artist
 ry\, always guided by the conviction that design can make people\nJacinto
  states "WORDLY is a series of paintings that explores the power of visua
 l representation of words. Each work is both text and image\, drawing atte
 ntion to how language shifts meaning when it transcends the page and ente
 rs the realm of visual art. By painting words\, Salcedo pretends to disrup
 t their familiarity\, asking viewers to not only read but to see language\
 , to feel its weight\, texture\, and presence. In a world where computer-g
 enerated text and templates are the norm. Salcedo explores the simplicity
 "\nThis exhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit\nprogram. Toronto Public Lib
 rary provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations a
 cross the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interes
 ts of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during\n
 Leaside Branch\nopen hours. Please check the Leaside Branch page before yo
 ur visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Artist: Jacinto Salcedo\;
  Title of Piece: HURT\; Medium: Acrylic\; Size/Dimensions: up to 20" x 20"
LOCATION:Leaside\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a46864648c98c3600a3e5bd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Managing Invasive Plants Around Your Home
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T193000
UID:69dd04048ddc1caf5f1c9755@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff for a presentation o
 n invasive plants commonly found around homes in Toronto. Learn how to ide
 ntify these species\, understand their impact\, and how to manage them.\nY
 ou’ll also get tips on supporting local biodiversity through enhancing n
 ative habitats. Perfect for gardeners\, homeowners\, and anyone interested
  in urban ecology.\nNo registration. Drop-in.\nThis program is part of TPL
 's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto P
 ublic Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dd04048ddc1caf5f1c9755
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
