SUMMARY:LinkedIn 101 with ACCES Employment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T150000
UID:6a4969be0e851028002f43da@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in this interactive workshop to learn how to utilize L
 inkedIn for your job search journey. You will learn strategies for targeti
 ng your LinkedIn profile\, forming connections\, keeping your account acti
 ve\, and reaching out to employers. Please bring your own personal device 
 to follow along.\nRegistration is encouraged on TPL website.\nDrop-ins wel
 come until capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4969be0e851028002f43da
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intro to D&D for Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260727T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260727T200000
UID:6a185e0a0c0f2c4503fb8a35@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Calling all adventurers!\nCome heed the call and learn the bas
 ics of Dungeons & Dragons. Learn the ins and outs of one of the worlds mos
 t popular Tabletop Roleplaying Games.\nNo experience required\, this is an
  absolute beginner friendly event.\nNo need to bring characters or charact
 er sheets. Pre-generated characters will be provided.\nThis program is int
 ended for a mature audience.\nRegistration is required. Please register on
 line or by calling 416-395-5720. Space is limited.
LOCATION:Downsview\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a185e0a0c0f2c4503fb8a35
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Data Science Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T193000
UID:6a10653dc7d3cd58005ae1d5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about Data Science? Let's take a free o
 nline course together in a welcoming space!\nTogether we will work through
  Cisco Networking Academy's Introduction to Data Science course over six w
 eeks\, where we'll be introduced to basic concepts\, including:\nIntroduct
 ory analytics\nData collection\nData storage\nAI and machine learning\nPar
 ticipants will learn together in a peer-supported environment through a le
 arning circle\, a lightly facilitated study group guided by library staff.
 \nLearners who successfully complete the course will earn a digital badge 
 and certificate of completion.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe person
 al information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library und
 er the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The info
 rmation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery an
 d evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can
  be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 
 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Computer Learning Centre
