UID:6a1a008bc6a1dc3d00d70f28@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:China Court Duo features three elegant Chinese traditional ins
 truments Pipa (Chinese lute) \, Xun (Globular vessel flute)\, and Dizi (Ba
 mboo flute). The two masterful musicians Wen Zhao (PIpa) and Yucheng Zhang
  (Xun and Dizi) focuses on performing Court repertoires and traditional fo
 lk music from the Ming and Qing dynasty\, the program includes spirited an
 cient poem repertories in China\, and Wen Zhao's recent composition for th
 e silk string Pipa Dynasty\, a suite work traces the history of the Pipa t
 hrough three of China's imperial dynasties.\nFor more information\, contac
 t the Arts Department at 416-393-7157.\nThursday\, July 23\, 2025\, 7\n:00
  – 8:00 p.m.\nBeeton Hall\, Toronto Reference Library
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1a008bc6a1dc3d00d70f28
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Business Inc Newcomer Series - Information Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T200000
UID:6a36efb216554cd59fca2524@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join our Fall 2026 Business Inc. Info Session to learn about t
 his 8-week program supporting Toronto entrepreneurs to launch and grow.\nD
 o you have a small business or idea and want tailored feedback and support
  to take it to the next level? Join the Business Inc. Program to connect w
 ith experienced mentors and other entrepreneurs that will help you grow.\n
 During eight weekly sessions\, entrepreneurs will learn business fundament
 als\, get clarity on the viability of their business ideas\, get feedback 
 and reviews from professional business advisors\, discuss with and learn f
 rom their peers\, and build a foundation for success.\nThe program will ru
 n weekly at Runnymede on Wednesday evenings from October 7 – November 25
 \, from 6 - 9pm.\nJoin us at our Information Session to learn more about t
 his program\, meet the instructor\, and ask any questions you may have abo
 ut your application.\nLearn about\nBusiness Inc.\n\, an eight-week busines
 s program offered in partnership with the Toronto Business Development Cen
 tre.\nRegistration is required. To register\, click\nhere\n.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a36efb216554cd59fca2524
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Create an Impactful Resume with ACCES Employment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T150000
UID:6a1c8e784407827f8aa1a7ee@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Employment experts will guide you through a step-by-step proce
 ss on creating a resume that stands out and gets you noticed by employers.
  Discover which information to include\, what to leave out\, professional 
 formatting tips\, and how to make your final product Applicant Tracking Sy
 stem (ATS)-friendly.\nRegistration is encouraged on TPL website.\nDrop-ins
  welcome until capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe p
 ersonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Librar
 y under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The
  information will only be used for event and program registration\, delive
 ry and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informatio
 n can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-59
 81\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1c8e784407827f8aa1a7ee
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google AI Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T160000
UID:6a17599543b41b3d00699e6b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about artificial intelligence or want to learn practic
 al AI skills for work and personal use? Join our staff-facilitated learnin
 g circle to complete the self-paced Google AI Essentials specialization.\n
 This 10-hour introductory-level specialization\, offered through Coursera\
 , is available for free to learning circle participants. It is made up of 
 five courses\, each containing four units that consist of short videos\, a
 rticles\, assignments and a short multiple-choice quiz.\nBy completing the
  specialization\,\nyou will learn:\nHow AI works\nHow to write effective p
 rompts\nHow to use generative AI tools responsibly\nHow to identify AI's p
 otential biases and avoid harm\nHow to stay up to date with AI news\nAfter
  you complete the course\, you earn a Google certificate and a badge to sh
 are with others\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary staf
 f for people who want to complete the Google AI Essentials specialization 
 together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work together thr
 ough course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to attending a
 ll four learning circle sessions.\nNo AI experience is required.\nHow to J
 oi\nn a Learning Circle:\nRegister once on the first session of this event
  series\, in order to attend all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid e
 mail address\n.\nA valid TPL library card is required for online circles
 .\nAttend all four sessions online via Zoom\, July 9\, 16\, 23\, and 30 fr
 om 2-4 PM.\nRegistration is a two-step procedure. First\, participants mus
 t complete their registration through this page. After this step\, library
  staff will follow up to request additional information in order to comple
 te the registration.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informa
 tion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Pub
 lic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wi
 ll only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluati
 on. Questions about how the library handles your information can be direct
 ed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge 
 Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a17599543b41b3d00699e6b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
