BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Alone in Density by Young Hee Sung
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T235959
UID:6a3acf1b3efcc843503590a1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Young Hee Sung is a multidisciplinary artist and the founder o
 f Laird Art Gallery in Toronto. Her practice blends Korean brush painting 
 and Western abstraction to explore impermanence\, memory\, and transformat
 ion. She has held solo exhibitions at Assembly Hall Gallery\, Laird Art Ga
 llery\, and Ajax City Hall\, and exhibited internationally in Los Angeles\
 , New Jersey\, and Seoul. She also curates collaborative projects that mer
 ge visual art with literature and community engagement.\nYoung Hee Sung is
  the founder of Brush Densityism\, a method of layering countless brushstr
 okes\, dots\, and lines to create dense fields of rhythm\, energy\, and co
 lor. Rooted in the intuitive vitality of Korean brush painting and the str
 uctured language of Western abstraction\, her work explores impermanence\,
  memory\, and transformation. Expanding into sculpture and text\, she crea
 tes participatory experiences where painting\, poetry\, and community conv
 erge in renewal.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogr
 am. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit the
 ir work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the di
 verse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit 
 can be viewed during North York Central Library open hours.\nFree. All are
  welcome.\nImage credit: Artist: Young Hee Sung\; Uphill.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd floor Gallery space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3acf1b3efcc843503590a1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Craft Club: Digital Creations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T170000
UID:69c56361b48451fc3c0b6ae4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Malvern Library's Craft Club runs twice a month on Tuesdays. 
 Basic supplies provided for learners.\nFirst session\n:\nJoin us in the Di
 gital Innovation Hub to make a crafting-related goodie to take home.\nRegi
 stration required.\nRegister in-person while participating in the previous
  month's session two. Any leftover spots are available to reserve online a
 fter the program ends.\nSecond session:\nDo you knit\, crochet\, hand-sew\
 , cross-stitch\, or embroider? Or are you looking to learn? Join us to st
 itch\, chat\, and have some fun while watching a cozy film.\nDrop-in.\nIn
 formation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is col
 lected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sect
 ions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for even
 t and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how 
 the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff a
 t\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 
 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c56361b48451fc3c0b6ae4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Word Basics 1: Write a Letter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T153000
UID:6a3af36a48c98c3600a1def1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Word for absolute beginners
 .\nIn this class\, you will:\n- Understand how to use Word’s Tabs\, Grou
 ps\, and Commands\n- Create\, save\, print and delete Word documents\n- Pr
 actice basic text formatting and style features\nUpon completion of this c
 lass\, you will be able to use Microsoft Word at a basic level.\nPrerequis
 ites: Basic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with 
 demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Learning Centre\, 1st Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3af36a48c98c3600a1def1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
