BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cyanotype Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T113000
UID:6a32d987154fb14b00222eed@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What materials and processes existed before Adobe Photoshop? J
 oin us for a hands-on analog image making workshop to create a Cyanotype. 
 The Cyanotype is a photographic printing technique sensitive to a limited 
 near ultraviolet and blue light spectrum. It involves layering objects and
  transparencies. All are welcome!\nWe will supply all materials\, but feel
  free to bring an object or 2D silhouette for a contact print.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Activity Room (first floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a32d987154fb14b00222eed
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T153000
UID:6a415f4e96ee38a44a9322b2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Bendale and its neighbourhood is home to a variety of tree
 s. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore the natural wo
 rld on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize different specie
 s and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\nChildren 
 under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nRegistration is requi
 red – please register online.\nThe tour will start and end at the Bendal
 e and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There ma
 y be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress and prepare a
 ccordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscree
 n\, water\, comfortable shoes). This program takes place rain or shine. In
  the event of severe inclement weather\, registrants will be notified of a
 n alternative date\n.\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\n
 program series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Ch
 apter.​
LOCATION:Bendale\, Meet in Auditorium\, lower level basement
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a415f4e96ee38a44a9322b2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
