BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Your Niche: Building A Business Around What Makes You Diff
 erent
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T200000
UID:6a2c8a981e67cd9cb3398f8a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:One of the biggest challenges entrepreneurs face is trying to 
 appeal to everyone. In reality\, the strongest businesses are often built 
 around a clearly defined audience and a unique point of difference.\nIn th
 is interactive workshop\, participants will explore how to identify their 
 target audience\, clarify their value proposition\, and position themselve
 s more effectively in the marketplace. Whether you're launching a new vent
 ure or refining an existing business\, you'll leave with practical tools t
 o help define what makes your business stand out.\nAll\n sessions are inte
 ractive and participants are encouraged to bring \nquestions related to th
 eir own business or entrepreneurial goals.\nMeet the Resident\n: Melanie C
 ruickshank is a founder and brand-side operator with over 15 years of expe
 rience building\, launching\, and scaling beauty and personal care brands.
  As the founder of da lish cosmetics\, she led everything from product dev
 elopment and retail strategy to e-commerce growth and national partnership
 s. Known for her hands-on\, no-nonsense approach\, Melanie brings a founde
 r’s accountability and a deep understanding of what it takes to build br
 ands that perform in market.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2c8a981e67cd9cb3398f8a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google AI Essentials: In Person Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T150000
UID:6a175bb02ea730c17ab23387@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about artificial intelligence or want to learn practic
 al AI skills for work and personal use? Join our staff-facilitated learnin
 g circle to complete the self-paced Google AI Essentials specialization.\n
 This 10-hour introductory-level specialization\, offered through Coursera\
 , is available for free to learning circle participants. It is made up of 
 five courses\, each containing four units that consist of short videos\, a
 rticles\, assignments and a short multiple-choice quiz.\nBy completing the
  specialization\,\nyou will learn:\nHow AI works\nHow to write effective p
 rompts\nHow to use generative AI tools responsibly\nHow to identify AI's p
 otential biases and avoid harm\nHow to stay up to date with AI news\nAfter
  you complete the course\, you earn a Google certificate and a badge to sh
 are with others\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary staf
 f for people who want to complete the Google AI Essentials specialization 
 together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work together thr
 ough course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to attending a
 ll four learning circle sessions.\nNo AI experience is required.\nHow to J
 oin\na Learning Circle:\nRegister once on the first session of this event 
 series\, in order to attend all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid em
 ail address\n.\nA valid TPL library card is required for online circles.
 \nAttend all four sessions in person at\nScarborough Civic Centre.\nRegist
 ration is a two-step procedure. First\, participants must complete their r
 egistration through this page. After this step\, library staff will follow
  up to request additional information in order to complete the registratio
 n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Scarborough Civic Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a175bb02ea730c17ab23387
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
